From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: puffin <noreply@tlspuffin>
Date: Sat, 6 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: guard SecureChannel delete/use against a channel freed
 on the CLO path (fix double-free / use-after-free)

Companion to Fix-securechannel-uaf.patch. This fixes the UAF that actually kills
with-bit fuzzing campaigns, precisely as described by the KNOWN ISSUE comment in
the Puffin harness (eventloop_puffin_tcp.c):

On a CloseSecureChannel (CLO) message, open62541's Service_CloseSecureChannel
frees the SecureChannel. The connection is then force-closed, and the delayed
CLOSING callback (TCP_delayedClose -> serverNetworkCallbackLocked) runs
deleteServerSecureChannel(context->channel) on the ALREADY-FREED channel ->
heap-use-after-free at ua_server_binary.c:118 (`while(channel->sessions)`), a
double-free. Symbolized campaign stack:
    deleteServerSecureChannel        ua_server_binary.c:118
    serverNetworkCallbackLocked      ua_server_binary.c:801  (CLOSING path)
    serverNetworkCallback -> TCP_delayedClose -> UA_EventLoopPuffin_run
Removing the harness force-close only moves the bug: the connection stays open and
a later receive hits UA_SecureChannel_loadBuffer on the freed channel (another
UAF). Because these fire during LibAFL's crash-handling window, the child exits
without a clean abort ("Storing state in crashed fuzzer instance did not work,
Child exited with: 0") and the whole campaign dies.

Fix (the vendor-side fix the harness comment prescribes -- "clear the
connection->channel association / guard loadBuffer"): before dereferencing or
deleting `channel` in serverNetworkCallbackLocked, verify it is still a registered
SecureChannel via puffinChannelStillRegistered(), which walks bpm->channels
comparing POINTERS ONLY (never dereferencing the possibly-freed channel). Guards
three sites: the CLOSING delete (skip if already gone -> no double-free), the
receive-path loadBuffer (skip if gone -> no UAF), and the message loop after
processSecureChannelMessage (which can free the channel mid-loop). The context is
still nulled after the CLOSING branch. No behavioural change for a live channel.
---
--- a/src/server/ua_server_binary.c
+++ b/src/server/ua_server_binary.c
@@ -732,6 +732,23 @@
  *   assigned to the appropriate UA_ServerConnection slot.
  * - The connection socket (active) initially points to the UA_ServerConnection
  *   slot and then gets assigned to the new SecureChannel instance. */
+/* Puffin harness-resilience: is `channel` still a registered SecureChannel?
+ * Compares by pointer only and never dereferences the (possibly already-freed)
+ * channel, so it is safe to call on a dangling pointer. Used to prevent the
+ * double-free / use-after-free that occurs when a CLO has freed the channel via
+ * Service_CloseSecureChannel but the connection / delayed-close still holds a
+ * stale reference to it (see KNOWN ISSUE in eventloop_puffin_tcp.c). */
+static UA_Boolean
+puffinChannelStillRegistered(UA_BinaryProtocolManager *bpm,
+                             const UA_SecureChannel *channel) {
+    UA_SecureChannel *c;
+    TAILQ_FOREACH(c, &bpm->channels, componentEntry) {
+        if(c == channel)
+            return true;
+    }
+    return false;
+}
+
 static void
 serverNetworkCallbackLocked(UA_ConnectionManager *cm, uintptr_t connectionId,
                             void *application, void **connectionContext,
@@ -798,9 +815,13 @@
         } else {
             /* A connection attached to a SecureChannel is closing. This is the
              * only place where deleteSecureChannel must be used. */
-            deleteServerSecureChannel(bpm, channel);
-            /* The channel is now freed. Clear the dangling context so a later
-             * callback on this connection id does not use-after-free it. */
+            /* The channel may already have been freed on the CLO path
+             * (Service_CloseSecureChannel), leaving *connectionContext dangling.
+             * Only delete it if it is still registered, to avoid a double-free. */
+            if(puffinChannelStillRegistered(bpm, channel))
+                deleteServerSecureChannel(bpm, channel);
+            /* Clear the (possibly dangling) context so a later callback on this
+             * connection id does not use-after-free it. */
             *connectionContext = NULL;
         }
 
@@ -850,6 +871,12 @@
     UA_DateTime nowMonotonic = el->dateTime_nowMonotonic(el);
 
     /* Process all complete messages */
+    /* The channel may have been freed on a prior CLO while the connection stayed
+     * open, leaving the local `channel` dangling. Skip unless still registered
+     * (pointer compare, no deref) to avoid use-after-free in loadBuffer. */
+    if(!puffinChannelStillRegistered(bpm, channel))
+        return;
+
     retval = UA_SecureChannel_loadBuffer(channel, msg);
     while(UA_LIKELY(retval == UA_STATUSCODE_GOOD)) {
         UA_MessageType messageType;
@@ -864,6 +891,11 @@
                                              messageType, requestId, &payload);
         if(copied)
             UA_ByteString_clear(&payload);
+        /* processSecureChannelMessage may have freed this channel (e.g. a CLO ->
+         * Service_CloseSecureChannel). Stop touching the now-dangling local
+         * `channel` before persistBuffer / the error path below. */
+        if(!puffinChannelStillRegistered(bpm, channel))
+            return;
     }
     retval |= UA_SecureChannel_persistBuffer(channel);
 
